      "summary": ": Wednesday 05/08 We are open today with a perfect winter's day on the cards. Today will be bluebird with cool temps and very light southwest winds. Grab an extra layer as it will start out cold. The grooming this morning is as good as it gets. Very cold overnight temps, fresh snowmaking, and fresh snow have all combined for some superb corduroy. Off piste snow is wind affected with some big drifts and some areas stripped by the wind. Main Basin lifts will be running from 08:30am with Captains, Soho, T-Bar, and Willows will follow from 09:00am Valley View lift will be closing at 3:35pm today. Ski out to cars will continue to be open. Passes: Everyone with a season's pass will need a picture on their profile/pass this year. If you're unsure if you have one, pop into any Guest Services location and they will be able to sort you out.",
